完整，回答逻辑链中每一步都解释出来。通过联网搜索让回答具体和精准。\nSLA的三级注意力权重分类策略，将attention block分为critical（top k_h%, 完整O(N²)计算）、marginal（中间，O(N)线性注意力）和negligible（bottom k_l%, 跳过）。相较于传统稀疏注意力的二级分类（保留/跳过），引入marginal层打破了稀疏度天花板：传统方法跳过中间值会引入显著误差（L1 error从3%跃至33%）…"},{"filename":"knowledge_notes/系统知识笔记/Iteration-Level Scheduling _ Selective Batching（迭代级调度）.md","basename":"Iteration-Level Scheduling _ Selective Batching（迭代级调度）","score":224.39698079754257,"foundWords":["block","blocking）。iteration-level","blocking","level"],"matches":[{"match":"Level","offset":13},{"match":"Level","offset":114},{"match":"level","offset":194},{"match":"blocking）。Iteration-level","offset":288},{"match":"Level","offset":541},{"match":"level","offset":1490},{"match":"level","offset":1600},{"match":"block","offset":1618},{"match":"level","offset":1915}],"excerpt":"## Iteration-Level Scheduling / Selective Batching（迭代级调度）\n术语是什么？回答尽量完整，回答逻辑链中每一步都解释出来。通过联网搜索让回答具体和精准。\nIteration-Level Scheduling 是 LLM serving 系统中的细粒度请求调度策略，由 Orca 系统首次提出。传统 serving 的 request-level batching 将不同请求 padding 到相同长度后批处理——padding token 浪费计算、已完成生成但未结束的请求需等待同批次慢请求（head-of-line blocking）。Iteration-level…"},{"filename":"knowledge_notes/算法知识笔记/Two-Level Quantization for Attention Map.md","basename":"Two-Level Quantization for Attention Map","score":222.88213817227154,"foundWords":["block","level"],"matches":[{"match":"Level","offset":7},{"match":"Level","offset":94},{"match":"Level","offset":324},{"match":"Level","offset":376},{"match":"Level","offset":431},{"match":"Level","offset":598},{"match":"// L","offset":765},{"match":"P̃ 后","offset":1336},{"match":"NVFP","offset":1455},{"match":"1×16","offset":1464}],"excerpt":"## Two-Level Quantization for Attention Map\n术语是什么？回答尽量完整，回答逻辑链中每一步都解释出来。通过联网搜索让回答具体和精准。\nTwo-Level Quantization 是 SageAttention3 提出的针对 attention map P（softmax 输出，值域 [0, 1]）的专用量化策略。由于 P 的值域极窄（[0, 1]），直接做 FP4 microscaling quantization 时，scale factor 的范围仅为 [0, 0.167]，导致 scale factor 在 E4M3 FP8 格式下仅能使用 280 个（…"},{"filename":"knowledge_notes/kernel知识笔记/Two-level Sparse Storage Format (BSR + Bitmap) for Sparse MHA.md","basename":"Two-level Sparse Storage Format (BSR + Bitmap) for Sparse MHA","score":213.78692066688976,"foundWords":["block单元；innertile","block单元","level"],"matches":[{"match":"level","offset":7},{"match":"level","offset":93},{"match":"block单元；InnerTile","offset":314},{"match":"level","offset":748}],"excerpt":"## Two-level Sparse Storage Format (BSR + Bitmap) for Sparse MHA\n术语是什么？通过联网搜索让回答具体和精准。\nTwo-level Sparse Storage Format是STOF提出的用于在GPU MHA kernel中统一表示任意sparse attention mask的两级存储格式，结合Block Compressed Sparse Row (BSR)和bitmap。该格式将mask矩阵按两级抽象组织：OuterTile (OT) 级——每个OT为64个8×8 InnerTile (IT)，OT作为coarse-grained s…"},{"filename":"knowledge_notes/系统知识笔记/Time-Slicing (NVIDIA GPU Application-Level Scheduling).md","basename":"Time-Slicing (NVIDIA GPU Application-Level Scheduling)","score":206.82437502393128,"foundWords":["blocks","level"],"matches":[{"match":"Level","offset":40},{"match":"level","offset":159},{"match":"level","offset":199},{"match":"blocks","offset":994}],"excerpt":"## Time-Slicing (NVIDIA GPU Application-Level Scheduling)\n术语是什么？回答尽量完整，回答逻辑链中每一步都解释出来。通过联网搜索让回答具体和精准。\nTime-Slicing 是 NVIDIA GPU 在多进程共享单 GPU 时默认的 application-level 调度机制（当 MPS 未启用时）。CUDA application-level scheduler 以固定时间片（约 2ms，本文在 Ampere RTX 3090 上证实）将 GPU 的全部计算资源（所有 SM、warp scheduler、执行核心）轮流分配给不同进程。在任意给定时刻，仅有一个进程的 kernel 在 GPU 上执行——不支持…"},{"filename":"knowledge_notes/算法知识笔记/Blockwise Token Selection.md","basename":"Blockwise Token Selection","score":206.3533106542102,"foundWords":["block","blockwise","blocking","block）","blocks","level"],"matches":[{"match":"Blockwise","offset":3},{"match":"Blockwise","offset":60},{"match":"block","offset":108},{"match":"level","offset":148},{"match":"blockwise","offset":194},{"match":"blockwise","offset":260},{"match":"blockwise","offset":305},{"match":"block","offset":359},{"match":"blockwise","offset":393},{"match":"blockwise","offset":438},{"match":"block","offset":550},{"match":"block","offset":575},{"match":"block","offset":593},{"match":"blocking","offset":602},{"match":"block","offset":672},{"match":"block","offset":711},{"match":"Blockwise","offset":801},{"match":"blocks","offset":870},{"match":"block","offset":913},{"match":"block","offset":933},{"match":"block","offset":1000},{"match":"block","offset":1143},{"match":"block","offset":1167},{"match":"block","offset":1620},{"match":"block）","offset":1812},{"match":"Blockwise","offset":1931},{"match":"block","offset":2076},{"match":"block","offset":2204},{"match":"block","offset":2310}],"excerpt":"## Blockwise Token Selection\n术语是什么？回答尽量完整，回答逻辑链中每一步都解释出来。\nBlockwise Token Selection 是一种在稀疏注意力中以**连续 token block 为粒度**选择重要 KV 子集参与注意力计算的方法。与 token-level selection（逐 token 选择，如 HashAttention）相比，blockwise selection 的核心优势在于：(1) 连续内存访问匹配 GPU 的 coalesced HBM 读取模式，blockwise 加载吞吐远高于 scatter/gather 的随机索引读取；(2…"},{"filename":"knowledge_notes/kernel知识笔记/Tile-Level Parallelism in Fused MoE Kernel.md","basename":"Tile-Level Parallelism in Fused MoE Kernel","score":204.76407920923228,"foundWords":["block","level"],"matches":[{"match":"Level","offset":8},{"match":"Level","offset":97},{"match":"/bloc","offset":430},{"match":"ssor","offset":1232}],"excerpt":"## Tile-Level Parallelism in Fused MoE Kernel\n术语是什么？回答尽量完整，回答逻辑链中每一步都解释出来。通过联网搜索让回答具体和精准。\nTile-Level Parallelism 是 FlashMoE 将大矩阵分解为细粒度、可独立调度的 tile 计算单元的策略。每个 128×64 tile 对应一个独立 task descriptor。MoE FFN (2×GEMM + activation) 和 Combine 统一为 task 抽象：t = (M, ⋆, φ)，执行 F_t(A, B, C, D) := C ← φ(A ⋆_t B + D)。⋆ 为 ·…"},{"filename":"knowledge_notes/系统知识笔记/Token-Level Dependency Tracking in Async MoE Serving（异步MoE推理中的Token级依赖追踪）.md","basename":"Token-Level Dependency Tracking in Async MoE Serving（异步MoE推理中的Token级依赖追踪）","score":192.66207779312214,"foundWords":["block","block#","level"],"matches":[{"match":"Level","offset":9},{"match":"Level","offset":128},{"match":"block#","offset":578}],"excerpt":"## Token-Level Dependency Tracking in Async MoE Serving（异步MoE推理中的Token级依赖追踪）\n术语是什么？回答尽量完整，回答逻辑链中每一步都解释出来。通过联网搜索让回答具体和精准。\nToken-Level Dependency Tracking 是 AMoE 系统中确保异步乱序执行语义正确性的机制。在传统同步 EP 中，barrier all-to-all 保证了所有 token 在进入下一层时已完全处理完毕。在 AEP 中，tokens 可能乱序到达和乱序执行——同一请求的不同 token 可能分布在不同的 µ-queue 中，以不同的顺序被调度执…"},{"filename":"knowledge_notes/算法知识笔记/Page-Level KV Cache Criticality Estimation (基于 Min_Max Key 元数据的 Page 级关键性估计).md","basename":"Page-Level KV Cache Criticality Estimation (基于 Min_Max Key 元数据的 Page 级关键性估计)","score":186.70122967669613,"foundWords":["block","level"],"matches":[{"match":"Level","offset":8},{"match":"Level","offset":131},{"match":"level","offset":1290},{"match":"个 thr","offset":2502},{"match":"，利用 w","offset":2527}],"excerpt":"## Page-Level KV Cache Criticality Estimation (基于 Min/Max Key 元数据的 Page 级关键性估计)\n术语是什么？回答尽量完整，回答逻辑链中每一步都解释出来。通过联网搜索让回答具体和精准。\nPage-Level KV Cache Criticality Estimation 是 Quest 的核心算法组件：利用 KV cache 每个 page 内 Key 向量的 per-channel 最小值 m_i 和最大值 M_i 作为紧凑元数据，结合当前 Query 向量 Q 计算每 page attention score 的数学上界，以此估计该 pag…"},{"filename":"knowledge_notes/kernel知识笔记/Stacked Co-location (堆叠共置).md","basename":"Stacked Co-location (堆叠共置)","score":168.44617649985906,"foundWords":["block","block就可以被调度到该sm","block_85,","block_84,","block_0,","block_0","block_1,","block_1","blocks在sm0内：","blocks在sm0内","blocks在sm内的垂直堆叠关系。在μshare的实验中，vectorized","blocks在sm内的垂直堆叠关系","blocks接近完成","blocksize，block就可以被调度到该sm。由于同一kernel的所有block有相同blocksize和资源需求，硬件scheduler自然倾向将它们填入相同的sm集合。现有系统（infless、orion、mps、mig）在inter-sm层面做spatial/temporal","blocksize","blocks，但这些blocks的hardware","blocks","level"],"matches":[{"match":"blocks","offset":113},{"match":"blocks","offset":143},{"match":"blocksize","offset":182},{"match":"blocksize","offset":231},{"match":"blocks，但这些blocks的hardware","offset":271},{"match":"blocks在SM内的垂直堆叠关系。在μShare的实验中，vectorized","offset":358},{"match":"blocksize","offset":422},{"match":"blocksize","offset":469},{"match":"blocks","offset":530},{"match":"blocks","offset":561},{"match":"block","offset":926},{"match":"block","offset":956},{"match":"block_0","offset":985},{"match":"block_1","offset":1033},{"match":"block_0,","offset":1088},{"match":"block_1,","offset":1102},{"match":"block_0","offset":1142},{"match":"block_84,","offset":1152},{"match":"block_1","offset":1167},{"match":"block_85,","offset":1177},{"match":"block","offset":1216},{"match":"blocks","offset":1238},{"match":"blocks接近完成","offset":1271},{"match":"blocks","offset":1328},{"match":"blocks在SM0内：","offset":1391},{"match":"level","offset":1740},{"match":"blocksize，block就可以被调度到该SM。由于同一kernel的所有block有相同blocksize和资源需求，硬件scheduler自然倾向将它们填入相同的SM集合。现有系统（INFless、Orion、MPS、MIG）在inter-SM层面做spatial/temporal","offset":1898},{"match":"blocksize","offset":2269}],"excerpt":"Stacked Co-location（堆叠共置）是指NVIDIA GPU硬件调度器的默认行为：当一个CUDA kernel被launch后，其多个blocks被顺序调度到SM cores，同一kernel的blocks因具有相同的资源需求而被\"堆叠\"在相同的SM内。由于kernel的blocksize通常远小于SM的总thread容量（如A40: 1536 threads, 默认blocksize 512-1024），一个SM可以同时容纳多个同kernel blocks，但这些blocks的hardware resource需求完全相同，导致SM内仅一种硬件资源被充分利用，其余资源闲置。\"Stacked\"一词强调同kernel blocks在SM内的垂直堆叠关系。在μShare的实验中，vectorized kernel (domina…"},{"filename":"knowledge_notes/系统知识笔记/Head-of-Line (HOL) Blocking in LLM Serving（LLM推理中的队首阻塞）.md","basename":"Head-of-Line (HOL) Blocking in LLM Serving（LLM推理中的队首阻塞）","score":145.48022339522615,"foundWords":["blocking","level"],"matches":[{"match":"Blocking","offset":22},{"match":"Blocking","offset":86},{"match":"blocking","offset":175},{"match":"blocking","offset":362},{"match":"blocking","offset":897},{"match":"level","offset":1248},{"match":"blocking","offset":1303},{"match":"level","offset":1544},{"match":"level","offset":1642},{"match":"level","offset":1723},{"match":"level","offset":1954}],"excerpt":"## Head-of-Line (HOL) Blocking in LLM Serving（LLM推理中的队首阻塞）\n术语是什么？\nHead-of-Line (HOL) Blocking 原是网络交换中的经典排队现象——当队首数据包因目的地拥塞无法转发时，其后所有数据包被阻塞无法前进，即使它们的目的地空闲。在 LLM Serving 中，HOL blocking 指迭代级 FCFS 调度下，先到达的长序列 BE（Best-Effort）请求占据 batch 前排位置，导致后到达的 LS（Latency-Sensitive）请求被阻塞在整个完整 decode iteration（300-400ms for Mixtral 8×7B）之后…"},{"filename":"knowledge_notes/kernel知识笔记/Recompute-Decode Fused Kernel (K1+K2 Fusion).md","basename":"Recompute-Decode Fused Kernel (K1+K2 Fusion)","score":137.16782562662308,"foundWords":["block","block划分k1/k2——k1和k2使用独立的thread","block划分k1","block组，避免warp","block组","block数按计算量比分","block分区**：不按warp而是按thread","block分区","block分配比例","blockidx.x","blockidx","block级别动态分配。","block级别动态分配","block,","block_id","blocks","level"],"matches":[{"match":"level","offset":130},{"match":"block级别动态分配。","offset":456},{"match":"block数按计算量比分","offset":779},{"match":"block,","offset":1859},{"match":"block分配比例","offset":2409},{"match":"block_id","offset":2626},{"match":"blockIdx.x","offset":2637},{"match":"blocks","offset":2658},{"match":"block_id","offset":2689},{"match":"blocks","offset":2703},{"match":"block","offset":2724},{"match":"block_id","offset":2817},{"match":"N个blo","offset":3189},{"match":"(block_","offset":3251},{"match":"1_bloc","offset":3265},{"match":"d block分区**：不按warp而是按thre","offset":3701},{"match":"d block划分K1/K2——K1和K2使用独立的thre","offset":3727},{"match":"d block组，避免wa","offset":3758},{"match":"l_bloc","offset":3805},{"match":"`个blo","offset":3813},{"match":"剩余blo","offset":3830},{"match":"r-lev","offset":4201},{"match":"d/blo","offset":4290}],"excerpt":"Recompute-Decode Fused Kernel（K1+K2融合kernel）是eLLM系统在layer-level execution中提出的CUDA kernel优化技术。它将两个原本串行执行的kernel融合为单一kernel launch：(1) K1——Recomputation kernel，为layer i+1的uncached旧token执行KV投影（GEMM操作，compute-intensive）；(2) K2——Decode kernel，用layer i的完整历史KV（cached+recomputed）对当前新token执行decode attention（memory-intensive）。融合后减少kernel launch overhead，提高SM utiliza…"}],"totalCount":50,"truncated":true},"effectiveQuery":"Triton block-level program_id tile autotuner path:knowledge_notes"}}}
